{"hits":{"hits":[{"updated":"2023-03-07T06:47:22.958177+00:00","metadata":{"citation_count":248,"publication_info":[{"journal_volume":"216","page_end":"276","year":1989,"page_start":"272","journal_title":"Phys.Lett.B"},{"page_end":"64","conference_record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/conferences/1343584"},"year":1990,"page_start":"52","parent_record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/304744"},"cnum":"C88-06-22"}],"authors":[{"full_name":"Frolov, Valeri P."},{"full_name":"Markov, M.A."},{"full_name":"Mukhanov, Viatcheslav F."}],"texkeys":["Frolov:1989pf"],"abstracts":[{"source":"Elsevier","value":"The internal structure of spacetime inside a black hole is investigated on the assumption that some limiting curvature exists. It is shown that the Schwarzchild metric inside a black hole can be attached to the de Sitter one at some spacelike junction surface which may represent a short transition layer. The possible fate of the de Sitter space which arises in the interior of a black hole in this model is discussed.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"Elsevier"}}],"control_number":278166,"dois":[{"value":"10.1016/0370-2693(89)91114-3"}],"titles":[{"title":"THROUGH A BLACK HOLE INTO A NEW UNIVERSE?"}]},"links":{"bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/278166?format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/278166?format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/278166?format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/278166?format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/278166?format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/278166?format=cv","citations":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A278166"},"id":"278166","created":"1989-05-18T00:00:00+00:00"}],"total":1},"links":{"self":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=j%20Phys.Lett.B%2C216%2C272&size=10&page=1&fields=control_number,titles,authors.full_name,publication_info,dois,abstracts,